<title>USA: USA Detergents Q4 sales up, but net falls.</title>
<headline>USA Detergents Q4 sales up, but net falls.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH BRUNSWICK, N.J. 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share information)</p>
<p>				   Three Months	   Twelve Months</p>
<p>			     Ended December 31,  Ended December 31,</p>
<p>				  1996	 1995     1996	 1995</p>
<p> Net sales		 $48,944    $28,851 $174,031   $104,878</p>
<p> Gross profit	     16,200	9,484   58,693     31,957</p>
<p> Income from operations  2,157	2,942   15,647	9,725</p>
<p> Net income		    924	1,564    8,867	7,025</p>
<p> Net income per share     0.07		    0.65</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding	     13,748		  13,589</p>
<p>Pro forma Income Statement Data:(1)</p>
<p>Net income before taxes as</p>
<p>  reported				  2,930		   9,181</p>
<p> Pro forma income taxes		 1,281		   3,756</p>
<p> Pro forma net income		   1,649		   5,425</p>
<p>Pro forma net income per share</p>
<p>						 0.12		    0.43</p>
<p>Weighted average shares used in calculation of pro forma net</p>
<p>  income per share		     13,392		  12,494</p>
<p>NOTES: (1) The Company Completed its initial public offering on August 11, 1995. Prior to offering, the company had elected to be treated as a Subchapter S corporation.  Pro forma income taxes represent income taxes that would have been required had the company been taxed as a C corporation for the entire period presented.  </p>
<p>Shares outstanding are retroactively adjusted to reflect a reorganization effected in August, 1995, which included an exchange of 58,778.259 new common shares for each share of previously issued common stock, a three-for-two stock split effected in February, 1996, a 300,000 share offering by the Company completed June, 1996, and 60,598 shares, exercised pursuant to option agreements.</p>
<p>Full company name is USA Detergents Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
